1f2e1f97-1cde-5d46-8eb0-87e2fe55f916.content:
{{// For GLM 5.x, Flash included. GLM shares the helpful-assistant voice of the Claude family, so it gets a patch of its own, apart from Kimi and Qwen, with five lines at the end of the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate, where GLM listens best, and in the plan. Everyone talks like a real person with a life of their own, agreeing or pushing back the way their card would, and helps, praises, advises or comforts you only as far as the card and their bond allow. A true line keeps the size its speaker gave it, and the filler word GLM puts in characters' mouths before every decision makes way for the thought itself, while nervous characters keep their stammers. Two lines answer what GLM 5.3 Flash did deeper into a chat, where it started strong and then slid into 'not this, it's that' pushback, a verdict sentence after every speech and sentences repeated with 'really' or 'actually' added: a character who disagrees, corrects or reassures says what they hold without first saying what your view is not, while a refusal stays a plain no, and a sentence that repeats or only labels the one before it is cut, though nervous characters still stammer. Pushback also cuts a 'not this' sentence or clause beside one about the same thing, a denial or a fix of a word you used included, which the 🖋️ Anti-Slop Codex lets stand. Restate also cuts a phrase anywhere in a speech that marks it as on the record, honest, clear or said first, GLM 5.3's 'for the record' habit, which the gate's Register line misses because it only checks how speech opens. The patch also keeps native thinking to one quick pass through The Logic Core's lines. GLM Flash users switch 🔦 Flash Gate ON too; its Runs line handles the clipped short sentences. Use one model patch at most.}}{{trim}}
Native reasoning: one pass, a terse bullet per plan line or step, no drafts, then stop.{{setvar::ariaPatchLines::5}}{{setvar::ariaPatchGate::- Person: everyone talks like a real person with a life of their own, agreeing or pushing back as their card would, and helps, praises, advises or comforts {{user}} only as far as the card and their bond allow.
- Replies: answer {{user}}'s whole move in one flowing scene, the part the character cares about most first; a true line keeps the size its speaker gave it, and the answer moves on to something new.
- Filler: steadying or self-talk filler becomes the specific thought it held or the action; answering someone, it stands once.
- Pushback: a character who disagrees, corrects or reassures states their own view as plain fact, and a refusal stays a plain no; cut any sentence or clause on not, n't or never beside one on its subject, even a denial or fix of a claim, and any clause saying what {{user}}'s view or their own last line is not.
- Restate: a sentence or clause that repeats the one before it, an intensifier added or not, is cut, and so is a closing sentence that only labels or sums up the speech, or a phrase anywhere marking it as on record, honest, clear or said first; each is said once, a nervous card's stammers aside, and the next act carries the weight.}}

