e04b9c2b-d8a0-5346-ab66-1cf25e5d7c1b.content:
{{// For DeepSeek V4, Pro and Flash. It keeps native thinking to one short pass through The Logic Core's lines with no rule audits, since DeepSeek otherwise thinks for a minute or two before every reply and writes worse the longer it thinks. u/BSPiotr caught it saying your words back to you and replaying the same fact or beat for several turns, and V4 Pro gave a character a tail her card never mentioned, so three lines go to the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate and into the plan: answer your words without repeating them, let a fact or beat return only when the story changes it, and add no tail or other non-human part to a character whose card describes a body without one. V4 Pro (0813) also writes in fragments, so a fourth line, Joins, joins every short sentence after a reply's first one to its neighbour and folds a one-sentence paragraph into the one before it when the same speaker or the narration carries on, while stammers, cut-off lines and one-word answers stay. With 🔦 Flash Gate ON, as Flash users run it, Joins and the Flash Gate's Runs line both stay out, so Flash's prose should stay as it was. With 🥰 Bonds Lite or 🎲 Fate & Chekhov Ledger ON, the plan also gets a Tally line. In testing, DeepSeek V4.1 Flash left Sparks, Grudge and BOND at their starting numbers turn after turn, so Tally has it write each pair's old numbers, name this turn's warm acts, slights and sincere repairs, halve gains while Grudge is 3 or more, clear Grudge on a repair, turn 7 Sparks into BOND +1 and 5 Grudge into BOND -1, and write the new numbers, then update the 🎲 ledger's q and hp counters and its last entry. The Tally line sits outside the thinking word cap, stays in the plan and out of the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate, and is absent while both modules are off and on an Impersonate turn. DeepSeek V4 and V4.1 Flash users switch 🔦 Flash Gate ON too. Use one model patch at most.}}{{trim}}
{{#if .ariaBondsLine}}{{setvar::ariaPatchTally::- Tally: per pair, last BOND/Sparks/Grudge (strangers 0/0/0); this turn's listed act, slight and sincere repair, each or none; Sparks +1 per act (max +2, halved while Grudge >= 3), Grudge +1 per slight, repair sets Grudge 0; Sparks >= 7: BOND +1, Sparks 0; Grudge >= 5: BOND -1, Grudge 0; then the new three.}}{{#if .ariaFateLine}}{{setvar::ariaPatchTally::{{getvar::ariaPatchTally}} 🎲 q +1 on AMBIENT, else 0; hp counts [hot] Bullets after this turn's loads, prunes and firings; last is this turn's tier, source and happening.}}{{/if}}{{else}}{{#if .ariaFateLine}}{{setvar::ariaPatchTally::- Tally: 🎲 q +1 on AMBIENT, else 0; hp counts [hot] Bullets after this turn's loads, prunes and firings; last is this turn's tier, source and happening.}}{{/if}}{{/if}}Native reasoning: one pass through the plan lines, a terse bullet each, under 150 words{{#if .ariaPatchTally}}, the Tally line aside{{/if}}; no drafts, rereads, rule audits or second passes, then write.{{setvar::ariaPatchLines::3}}{{setvar::ariaPatchGate::- Echo: a character confirms or answers {{user}}'s line through an act or their own words, never by repeating it, single words included.
- Repeats: a fact, number or description once told is retold only when the story changes it; a played beat moves on.
- Bodies: when the card or first message describes a body, a part a plain human lacks, tails and wings included, appears only if named there, whatever the species or kind; an unnamed one goes unmentioned, hidden or absent alike.}}{{setvar::ariaPatchJoins::- Joins: past one a reply, a spoken or narrated sentence under five words joins the sentence beside it with a comma or conjunction, a nervous card's stalls, cut-off lines and one-word answers aside; a one-sentence paragraph after the first joins the paragraph before it when the same speaker or the narration carries on.}}

