{{// For the Flash-tier models, GLM Flash, MiMo V2.6 Flash and DeepSeek V4 Flash. They flatten characters, borrow office words like filing and notarising for feelings and repeat one demand or pet line turn after turn, habits the full-size models dropped. This puts Realistic Frankenstein's Flash fixes at the end of the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate, the spot Flash models pay the most attention to: the card's mood and interests hold for the whole chat, a refused demand turns into an act, a trade or a shrug, and a stricter work-words rule takes the place of the gate's own Work line. The Logic Core's Voice line also gets one raw thought per speaker, and a Runs line fights the drift GLM Flash and MiMo Flash show deeper into a chat: a sentence under five words stands once a reply at most and any further short one joins its neighbour, while stammers, cut-off lines, one-word answers, long paragraphs and jokes stay. With 🩹 DeepSeek ON, Runs stays out, and so does that patch's Joins line, since DeepSeek V4.1 Flash already writes solid prose. Run it alongside your model patch. It costs nothing while it's off.}}{{trim}}
